  <section class="story-section">
    <h2>Why It Matters</h2>
    <p>
      Classical IK assumes the kinematic model matches the robot. Real arms diverge. An
      always-learning adapter turns that mismatch into something the controller can keep
      eating, instead of something that forces a recalibration ritual or tighter (and more
      expensive) machining.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
